  "id": "DrugBank_DB00051 - MONDO_grouped_5306_20655",
  "verbalization": "Adalimumab, a monoclonal antibody, is implicated in the treatment of Ankylosing Spondylitis through a series of interconnected indications. The evidence suggests that Adalimumab may exert its therapeutic effect by targeting inflammatory pathways that are also involved in other inflammatory conditions, such as Inflammatory Bowel Disease and Juvenile Arthritis. This is supported by the observed relationships with Certolizumab Pegol and Etanercept, both of which are known to inhibit inflammatory processes and are used in the treatment of Ankylosing Spondylitis. The shared mechanism of action, involving the inhibition of tumor necrosis factor (TNF) or similar inflammatory mediators, appears to be a key factor in the cross-indication between Adalimumab and Ankylosing Spondylitis. The evidence from multiple paths indicates a potential for Adalimumab to be repurposed for Ankylosing Spondylitis, likely through its ability to modulate inflammatory responses that are common across these conditions.",
